  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>Schizolecis guntheri comes from the coastal rainforests of southeastern Brazil. The natural habitats there are much affected by the growing human population, and water pollution in particular is a growing threat to the aquatic animals. Many endemic fish are in danger of extinction.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>A species-specific tank is preferred. It does not need to be very large, as this tiny species (maximum length reported 5 cm) does not need spacious aquariums.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>The tank should be well illuminated so that algae can grow. These fish originate from relatively cool, fast running waters, so a regular water change of 50-70% is highly recommended. The water should be well filtered, and the tank should be placed in a cool room.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish originate from relatively cool waters (maximum 23°C).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>Schizolecis feed mainly on aufwuchs, although all types of regular small fish food are readily accepted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/schizolecis_guntheri_and_lg4_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Schizolecis: ancient Greek, \"with splitted platelet\", referring to an anatomical feature. guntheri: dedicated to Albert Günther (1830–1914), one of the most important ichthyologists.</p>"
    }
  ],
